title: A Strike Breaks Out
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and c_strike_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.c_strike_timer = 3;
Q.month_actions += 1;
var trades = {
    berlin: 'the metalworkers at the Siemens and AEG works',
    hamburg: 'the dockers and shipyard workers of the port',
    bremen: 'the shipyard workers at the Weser yard',
    ruhr: 'the miners of the Ruhr pits',
    saxony: 'the textile workers of Chemnitz and Plauen',
    thuringia: 'the porcelain and toy workers of the Thuringian forest',
    bavaria: 'the railway workshops of Munich',
    halle: 'the chemical workers at Leuna and the miners of the Mansfeld copper pits'
};
var d = Q.districts[Math.floor(Math.random() * Q.districts.length)];
Q.c_strike_district = d;
Q.c_strike_district_name = Q.district_names[d];
Q.c_strike_trade = trades[d];
!}
frequency: 250
is-card: true
tags: movement

= A Strike Breaks Out

In [+ c_strike_district_name +], [+ c_strike_trade +] have walked out. [? if inflation >= 40 : Their wages are worth less every week. ?][? if inflation < 40 : They want the eight-hour day kept, the food allowance raised and the foremen who informed on them in the war sacked. ?] The union officials want it settled quickly. Our members are on the strike committee.

- @fund: Fund the strike committee.
- @political: Turn it into a political strike.
- @union: Let the union negotiate, and keep our people on the committee.
- @easy_discard

@fund
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The strikers hold out longer, and the district remembers who fed them.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
var d = Q.c_strike_district;
Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] += 8;
Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.05;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.militancy += 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

The party's money buys soup and coal for the strikers' families. After three weeks the employers give way on most of the demands.

@political
subtitle: Strikers' demands against the government itself. Militancy rises; so does repression. The Left's line.
on-arrival: {!
var d = Q.c_strike_district;
Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] += 4;
Q.militancy += 8;
Q.repression += 5;
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.stability -= 2;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 4;
if (!Q.ultraleft_gone) {
    Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 4;
}
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Our speakers add the demands of the whole class: release the prisoners, disarm the Freikorps, the councils to power. The strike spreads to two more works before the police break it up.

@union
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A modest settlement. The workers keep their gains and their trust in us. The Right approves.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids work inside the old unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_union_work == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.spd_relation += 2;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 3;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

The union signs a compromise. Our comrades on the committee make sure the strikers know which parts of it they fought for.
